
%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:floodnet@

%9Parameters:%9

    STATUS:     Displays whether the protection is enabled, the number of
                flood attempts today, the total number of blocked messages,
                the size of the message window, the number of active blocks,
                and the thresholds and time windows in use.
    RESET:      Sets the 'flood attempts today' and 'total messages
                blocked' counters to zero. Active blocks are kept.
    DETAILS:    Lists the active blocks: the blocked message texts, the
                servers whose CTCP requests are ignored and the channels
                whose nick changes are hidden, each with its remaining time.
    HELP:       Prints a short list of the subcommands and settings.

    Without any parameter, the status is displayed.

%9Description:%9

    Controls the anti-floodnet module, which hides floods sent by many
    clients at once (floodnets). It is loaded at startup by default (it is
    listed in the autoload_modules setting). It watches three things:

    Private messages sent to your nick, on all servers together, during the
    last anti_floodnet_time_window seconds. When anti_floodnet_tilde_threshold
    different users without ident (a '~' in the user name) sent them, the
    message is dropped and every text in the window is blocked for
    anti_floodnet_block_duration seconds. When at least 5 messages are in the
    window and anti_floodnet_duplicate_threshold different users sent the
    same text, that text is blocked and messages with it are dropped. One
    person pasting lines or repeating a line never counts as a flood, and
    messages from someone you already have a query with are never checked.
    Either case starts protection mode: while it is on, every private
    message from a user without ident or with a blocked text is dropped,
    and each one extends the block of its text.

    CTCP requests: when anti_floodnet_ctcp_threshold of them arrive from a
    server within anti_floodnet_time_window seconds, all CTCP requests on that
    server are ignored for anti_floodnet_block_duration seconds.

    Nick changes: when anti_floodnet_nickchange_threshold nick changes happen
    on a channel within anti_floodnet_nickchange_window seconds, the nick
    change messages of users on that channel are hidden for
    anti_floodnet_block_duration seconds, extended by every further change.

    Unless anti_floodnet_notices is OFF, a notice is printed in the active
    window when protection mode starts, every anti_floodnet_notice_interval
    seconds while it lasts, and when it ends - when no message is left in
    the window and every block has expired.

    Settings and their defaults (a number set to 0 also means the default):

        anti_floodnet_enabled                 ON
        anti_floodnet_tilde_threshold         5
        anti_floodnet_duplicate_threshold     3
        anti_floodnet_ctcp_threshold          5
        anti_floodnet_nickchange_threshold    5
        anti_floodnet_time_window             5 (seconds)
        anti_floodnet_nickchange_window       3 (seconds)
        anti_floodnet_block_duration          60 (seconds)
        anti_floodnet_notice_interval         60 (seconds)
        anti_floodnet_notices                 ON

%9Examples:%9

    /FLOODNET
    /FLOODNET DETAILS
    /FLOODNET RESET
    /SET anti_floodnet_ctcp_threshold 10
    /SET anti_floodnet_notices OFF

%9See also:%9 IGNORE, SET

